    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, just had a cow come out of rumenotomy this morning. need a solid protocol for the next few days. what should i be looking for regarding infection and how should i handle the diet reintroduction? cheers",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In the coming days, closely monitor the incision site for signs of infection like excessive swelling, redness, or discharge. Watch for signs of systemic illness such as lethargy, fever, or poor appetite, which could also indicate infection. Gradually reintroduce feed, starting with easily digestible forage and small amounts of high-quality grain, monitoring for digestive upset before progressing. Ensure the cow has constant access to fresh, clean water throughout the recovery process.",
