    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i'm mostly worried about things going wrong internally though. like i can't see what's happening inside the rumen, so how do i know if there's some kind of hidden bacterial buildup or something \"lurking\" in there that's going to cause a problem later? any specific red flags for internal issues?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Internal ruminal issues can be subtle initially, so be very vigilant about the cow's overall clinical signs. Key red flags include persistent, unexplained diarrhea, changes in manure consistency or odor, or regurgitation/bloating, especially when starting the diet. Also, watch for decreased rumination or abnormal gas production, as these can point to issues like ruminal acidosis or bacterial imbalance. If these signs persist despite supportive care, veterinary consultation is crucial.",
      "source": "target",
